### Where to check stock
In both, browser for feedback and server as the real guard

### Server validation function
function validateOrder(body, stockByItem) {
  if (!body.name || body.name.trim().length < 2) return 'name_invalid';
  if (!/^[6-9][0-9]{9}$/.test(String(body.phone))) return 'phone_invalid';
  const stock = stockByItem[body.itemId];
  if (stock === undefined) return 'item_unknown';
  const qty = Number(body.quantity);
  if (!Number.isInteger(qty) || qty < 1) return 'quantity_invalid';
  if (qty > stock) return 'quantity_above_stock';
  return null;
}

### Error message for a bad phone
Please enter a 10-digit mobile number, like 9876543210, so we can call you when your order is ready.

### Error message for too many items
Only 12 are left in stock. Please choose 12 or fewer, or pick another item.

### Your reasoning
The browser should still check empty fields and phone length because it gives instant, friendly feedback. The server repeats the phone, item and stock checks since someone can send a request without the page, and stock is the shop's money. I kept messages polite and told the customer what number to type.

