### Evidence for the assistant
I will paste: steps (open page, pick Saturday 5pm, press Book), expected (row in bookings), actual (message shows, no row), and the server error line. I will replace the DB password, API keys and any parent phone numbers with placeholders like <DB_PASSWORD> and <PHONE> first.

### Fixed handler
app.post('/api/bookings', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    await db.query(
      'INSERT INTO bookings (slot_id, parent_id) VALUES ($1, $2)',
      [req.body.slotId, req.session.userId]
    );
    res.status(201).json({ ok: true, message: 'Booking confirmed' });
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('booking save failed', err.message);
    res.status(500).json({ ok: false, message: 'We could not save your booking. Please try again.' });
  }
});

### Your reasoning
The bug was that the handler sent the confirmation without waiting for the insert, and swallowed the error, so I reproduced it first and then fixed the order. I remove secrets and phone numbers because a pasted key can be stored or leaked, and I test the assistant's theory with a real booking instead of trusting it.

