### Role names
parent and tutor

### Reply for someone else's booking
404 Not Found, hiding that it exists

### Access-check function
function canViewBooking(user, booking) {
  if (!user || !booking) return false;
  if (user.role === 'tutor') return true;
  return user.role === 'parent' && booking.parentId === user.id;
}

### Where the check runs
In the server route for every read, change and cancel, because buttons can be skipped by editing the address or sending a request.

### Your reasoning
Login only proves Meera is Meera, but permission is a separate question: is this booking hers. I chose 404 so a stranger cannot learn which booking numbers exist, and the tutor role is the one exception. The function runs on the server so changing the address or hiding buttons makes no difference.

